window.DOCS["6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c"]={"id":"6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c","summary":{"title_zh":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 財務機制之非正式文本","what":"這份文本是由第一工作小組（Working Group I）提出的非正式文本，內容涵蓋全球環境基金（GEF）第九次增資期（2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月）的認捐與資金需求、GEF 效能改善措施，以及全球生物多樣性綱要基金（GBFF）的運作與盤點檢討。","points":["[敦促][要求]已開發國家締約方，並邀請其他自願承擔已開發國家義務之締約方及其他國家，為全球環境基金第九次增資捐款，以支持綱要的全面落實。","歡迎全球環境基金理事會的報告，並歡迎第九次增資期方案將 35% 資源配置於生物多樣性重點領域，目標至少 70% 經費投入生物多樣性（依里約標記方法）。","要求全球環境基金加速提升效能，包括改善環境公約間的整合、促進私部門融資、減少交易成本並簡化取得程序，以及深化對原住民族與地方社區的可及支持，包括為其 20% 整體組合目標制定指引。","歡迎全球環境基金在第九次增資期設立原住民族與地方社區保育倡議，並以期望目標 20% 資源支持原住民族與地方社區，以期望基準 35% 加強支持低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家。","要求執行秘書為第十次增資期（2030–2034 年）撰寫資金需求完整評估報告，並視資源可用性辦理（第 39(b) 段）；另就全球生物多樣性綱要基金的盤點檢討進行準備（第 22 段，仍在括號內）。","注意到已收到 45 個合格締約方的資金需求資訊，但提交數量有限，因此可供評估的資訊仍不足（第 29、31 段）。"],"open":["[第 1 至 3 段：對第九次增資約 39 億美元認捐的措辭（「歡迎」、「確認」或「注意到並感謝」），以及是否以「深切關切」表示 27% 的減幅，或僅指出資源仍不足；認捐數字待 2026 年 10 月更新]","[第 4 段：已開發國家締約方的捐款是「敦促」還是「要求」]","[第 11 段與第 12(g) 段：全球環境基金理事會治理是否須確保民主、透明，並促進原住民族與地方社區、婦女及青年的完整有效參與與決策參與]","[第 12(d)–(f) 段與註 9、11、12：資源分配公式是否納入以過去撥款績效為基礎的要素、是否避免使能力受限國家受不利影響，以及原住民族與地方社區是否以直接取得（direct access）方式取得資金]","[第 20 段（GBFF 的要求，包括擴大出資者基礎、共同融資條件、簡化程序）及第 22 段（GBFF 盤點檢討準備工作）整段仍在括號內，各方意見未定]","[附件 II、附件 III 的評估與檢視範圍、準則與程序（包括直接取得與資源分配檢視），以及第 34、36 段是否採用，仍未定案]"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p001.md","en":[{"t":"Agenda item 8 (b)"},{"t":"Resource mobilization and financial"},{"t":"mechanism: resource mobilization"},{"t":"Working Group I"},{"t":"Financial mechanism"},{"t":"Non-paper"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties,"},{"t":"Recalling its decisions 15/15 of 19 December 2022 and 16/33 of 27 February 2025 pertaining to the assessment of funding needed by all eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition for the implementation of the Convention on Biological Diversity 1 and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2026–June 2030), Recalling also the four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund contained in annex I to decision 16/33,"},{"t":"Recognizing that the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework2 is relevant to all biodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral environmental agreements and the mandate of the Global Environment Facility,"},{"t":"[1. [Welcomes][Acknowledges][Notes with appreciation] the pledges made as at 30 May 2026 for the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund by participant countries, namely, Australia, Austria, Belgium, Brazil, Canada, China, Côte d’Ivoire, France, Germany, India, Ireland, Italy, Japan, Luxembourg, Mexico, Netherlands (Kingdom of the), New Zealand, Norway, Slovenia, South Africa, Switzerland and Uzbekistan, which amounted to approximately 3.9 billion United States dollars, using the agreed reference exchange rates for the replenishment period;3]"},{"t":"[2. Notes with concern that the amount of 3.9 billion dollars is contributed by only 50 per cent of developed country Parties, and appreciates the contributions of developing country Parties, namely, Brazil, China, Côte d’Ivoire, India, Mexico, South Africa and Uzbekistan;4] [3. [Notes with deep concern] that [the negotiations for the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund concluded with a reduction of 27 per cent compared with the eighth replenishment period and that such a reduction comes at a time when Parties are expected to accelerate the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework][the overall level of resources remains insufficient in the light of the scale of needs to implement the Convention on Biological Diversity and its Protocols and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, in particular Target 19 (a);]]5"},{"t":"1 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"2 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"3 To be updated in October 2026."},{"t":"4 To be updated in October 2026."},{"t":"5 Operative paragraphs 1 to 3 were considered at the seventh meeting of the Subsidiary Body on Implementation (see"},{"t":"recommendation 7/3). Recommendation 6/2, adopted at its sixth meeting, also contained a paragraph on the topic of the ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (para. 6), but that paragraph was not discussed at that meeting. It is the understanding of the Secretariat that paragraphs 1 to 3 above reflect the discussions of the Subsidiary Body on the subject and therefore supersede the not-negotiated paragraph 6 in recommendation 6/2. As a result, that paragraph has not been included in the present draft decision. For reference, it read as follows: “[Reiterates its appreciation to developed country Parties, other Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of developed country Parties and other donors that contributed actively to the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund and the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund in support of eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, [the most environmentally vulnerable country Parties,] and Parties with economies in transition;]”."}],"blocks":[{"md":"議程項目 8 (b)\n資源動員與財務機制：資源動員\n第一工作小組","html":"<p>議程項目 8 (b)<br />\n資源動員與財務機制：資源動員<br />\n第一工作小組</p>","en":[0,1,2,3]},{"md":"財務機制\n非正式文件（Non-paper）","html":"<p>財務機制<br />\n非正式文件（Non-paper）</p>","en":[4,5,6]},{"md":"締約方大會，","html":"<p>締約方大會，</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"**回顧**其 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/15 以及 2025 年 2 月 27 日之決議 16/33，該等決議涉及評估所有符合條件之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方）為執行《生物多樣性公約》$^1$及其議定書，於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間（2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月）所需之資金；","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/15 以及 2025 年 2 月 27 日之決議 16/33，該等決議涉及評估所有符合條件之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方）為執行《生物多樣性公約》<sup>1</sup>及其議定書，於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間（2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月）所需之資金；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"**亦回顧**決議 16/33 附件一所載，關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，該公約及其議定書之四年期、以成果為導向的生物多樣性計畫優先事項框架；","html":"<p><strong>亦回顧</strong>決議 16/33 附件一所載，關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，該公約及其議定書之四年期、以成果為導向的生物多樣性計畫優先事項框架；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"**認識到**《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要$^2$》與所有生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議，以及全球環境基金之職權相關；","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong>《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要<sup>2</sup>》與所有生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議，以及全球環境基金之職權相關；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"[1. [歡迎][承認][表示感謝地注意到] 參與國截至 2026 年 5 月 30 日為全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所做出之承諾，即：澳洲、奧地利、比利時、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、法國、德國、印度、愛爾蘭、義大利、日本、盧森堡、墨西哥、荷蘭（王國）、紐西蘭、挪威、斯洛維尼亞、南非、瑞士及烏茲別克，其金額依增資期間之議定參考匯率計算，總計約 39 億美元；$^3$]","html":"<p>[1. [歡迎][承認][表示感謝地注意到] 參與國截至 2026 年 5 月 30 日為全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所做出之承諾，即：澳洲、奧地利、比利時、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、法國、德國、印度、愛爾蘭、義大利、日本、盧森堡、墨西哥、荷蘭（王國）、紐西蘭、挪威、斯洛維尼亞、南非、瑞士及烏茲別克，其金額依增資期間之議定參考匯率計算，總計約 39 億美元；<sup>3</sup>]</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"[2. **憂心地注意到** 39 億美元之金額僅由 50% 的已開發國家締約方所貢獻，並**歡迎**開發中國家締約方之貢獻，即：巴西、中國、象牙海岸、印度、墨西哥、南非及烏茲別克；$^4$]","html":"<p>[2. <strong>憂心地注意到</strong> 39 億美元之金額僅由 50% 的已開發國家締約方所貢獻，並<strong>歡迎</strong>開發中國家締約方之貢獻，即：巴西、中國、象牙海岸、印度、墨西哥、南非及烏茲別克；<sup>4</sup>]</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"[3. [**深切憂心地注意到**] [全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之談判結果，與第八期增資期間相比減少了 27%，且此種減少發生在締約方預期應加速執行《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之際][鑑於執行《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》（特別是目標 19 (a)）之需求規模，整體資源水準仍顯不足；]]$^5$","html":"<p>[3. [<strong>深切憂心地注意到</strong>] [全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之談判結果，與第八期增資期間相比減少了 27%，且此種減少發生在締約方預期應加速執行《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之際][鑑於執行《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》（特別是目標 19 (a)）之需求規模，整體資源水準仍顯不足；]]<sup>5</sup></p>","en":[10]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[11]},{"md":"$^1$ 聯合國，《條約集》，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^2$ 決議 15/4，附件。\n$^3$ 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。\n$^4$ 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。\n$^5$ 執行附屬機構第七次會議已審議執行段落 1 至 3（參見建議 7/3）。其第六次會議所通過之建議 6/2 亦包含一段關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資主題之段落（第 6 段），但該段落未在該次會議中進行討論。秘書處之理解為，上述第 1 至 3 段反映了附屬機構就該主題之討論，因此取代了建議 6/2 中尚未經談判之第 6 段。因此，該段落未包含在本決議草案中。供參考，其原文如下：「[重申對已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之其他締約方，以及為支持符合條件之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家、[環境最脆弱之締約方] 以及經濟轉型中締約方）而對全球生物多樣性綱要基金及全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資做出積極貢獻之其他捐助者，表示感謝；]」。","html":"<p><sup>1</sup> 聯合國，《條約集》，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>2</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。<br />\n<sup>3</sup> 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。<br />\n<sup>4</sup> 將於 2026 年 10 月更新。<br />\n<sup>5</sup> 執行附屬機構第七次會議已審議執行段落 1 至 3（參見建議 7/3）。其第六次會議所通過之建議 6/2 亦包含一段關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資主題之段落（第 6 段），但該段落未在該次會議中進行討論。秘書處之理解為，上述第 1 至 3 段反映了附屬機構就該主題之討論，因此取代了建議 6/2 中尚未經談判之第 6 段。因此，該段落未包含在本決議草案中。供參考，其原文如下：「[重申對已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之其他締約方，以及為支持符合條件之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家、[環境最脆弱之締約方] 以及經濟轉型中締約方）而對全球生物多樣性綱要基金及全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資做出積極貢獻之其他捐助者，表示感謝；]」。</p>","en":[12,13,14,15,16]}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p002.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"4. [Urges][Requests] developed country Parties, and invites other Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of developed country Parties and other countries, to make contributions for the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund in support of the full implementation of the Framework and in accordance with the provisions of Article 20 of the Convention;"},{"t":"5. Welcomes the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;6"},{"t":"6. Also welcomes the improved disaggregation of co-financing by source in the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility and encourages the Facility to continue to enhance the transparency and granularity of future reporting on the various sources of co-financing;"},{"t":"7. Notes with appreciation that the programming directions for the ninth replenishment period have been designed to deliver on all elements of the four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period adopted by the Conference of the Parties at its sixteenth meeting,7 reflecting the effective response to the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"8. Welcomes the allocation of 35 per cent of the ninth replenishment resources to the biodiversity focal area, which is the largest focal area, and the aim of committing at least 70 per cent of funding to biodiversity over that period, according to the Rio marker methodology of the Development Assistance Committee of the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development;"},{"t":"9. Also welcomes the inclusion in the programming directions and policy"},{"t":"recommendations of the Global Environment Facility for the ninth replenishment period of the indigenous people and local community conservation initiative, 8 an aspirational target of programming 20 per cent of resources to support indigenous peoples and local communities and strengthened support to least developed countries and small island developing States, with an aspirational benchmark of 35 per cent for those countries, as well as the introduction of the aspirational target of programming 25 per cent to mobilize private capital;"},{"t":"10. Further welcomes the establishment of the Ad Hoc Governance Working Group of the Council of the Global Environment Facility under the ninth replenishment of the Facility, in response to decision 16/33;"},{"t":"[11. Requests the Council of the Global Environment Facility to take into account the criteria [set out in paragraph 21 of decision 16/34 of 27 February 2025] [and decision 17/--], ensuring a democratic and transparent system of governance that is fair, equitable, inclusive, efficient and representative[, while facilitating the full and effective participation of indigenous people and local communities, women and youth];]"},{"t":"12. Requests the Global Environment Facility to accelerate efforts to further strengthen its effectiveness, including by:"},{"t":"(a) Improving integration pathways, approaches and integrated programmes that deliver system-wide environmental benefits to improve synergies among environmental conventions, while ensuring that such programmes take into account their respective mandates, remain country-driven, responsive to national circumstances and priorities, and implemented through meaningful engagement with national executing agencies from recipient countries;"},{"t":"(b) Enabling and facilitating private sector financing aligned with the objectives of the Convention through its blended finance programme funding window and the provision of predictable support to eligible Parties, with a view to developing projects and programmes that enable greater"},{"t":"6 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1."},{"t":"7 Decision 16/33, annex I."},{"t":"8 Building on previous iterations of the Inclusive Conservation Initiative at an expanded level of 100 million dollars,"},{"t":"2/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"4.\n[敦促][請求] 已開發國家締約方，並邀請其他自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之國家，為全球環境基金信託基金第九次增額提供貢獻，以支持《綱要》之全面實施，並符合《公約》第 20 條之規定；","html":"<p>4.<br />\n[敦促][請求] 已開發國家締約方，並邀請其他自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之國家，為全球環境基金信託基金第九次增額提供貢獻，以支持《綱要》之全面實施，並符合《公約》第 20 條之規定；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"5.\n**歡迎**全球環境基金理事會提交予第十七次締約方大會之報告；⁶","html":"<p>5.<br />\n<strong>歡迎</strong>全球環境基金理事會提交予第十七次締約方大會之報告；⁶</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"6.\n亦**歡迎**全球環境基金理事會報告中，針對共同融資來源進行更佳的分類，並**鼓勵**基金持續提升未來關於各類共同融資來源報告之透明度與細緻度；","html":"<p>6.<br />\n亦<strong>歡迎</strong>全球環境基金理事會報告中，針對共同融資來源進行更佳的分類，並<strong>鼓勵</strong>基金持續提升未來關於各類共同融資來源報告之透明度與細緻度；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"7.\n**注意到**第九次增額期間的規劃方向，已旨在達成締約方大會於第十六次會議所採納之、為期四年且以成果為導向的《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性優先事項框架之所有要素，⁷ 並反映了對締約方大會所提供指引之有效回應；","html":"<p>7.<br />\n<strong>注意到</strong>第九次增額期間的規劃方向，已旨在達成締約方大會於第十六次會議所採納之、為期四年且以成果為導向的《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性優先事項框架之所有要素，⁷ 並反映了對締約方大會所提供指引之有效回應；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"8.\n**歡迎**將第九次增額資源之 35% 分配至生物多樣性重點領域（此為最大之重點領域），且根據經濟合作暨發展組織開發援助委員會之里約標記法（Rio marker methodology），其目標是在該期間內將至少 70% 的資金投入於生物多樣性；","html":"<p>8.<br />\n<strong>歡迎</strong>將第九次增額資源之 35% 分配至生物多樣性重點領域（此為最大之重點領域），且根據經濟合作暨發展組織開發援助委員會之里約標記法（Rio marker methodology），其目標是在該期間內將至少 70% 的資金投入於生物多樣性；</p>","en":[5,6]},{"md":"9.\n亦**歡迎**在全球環境基金第九次增額期間的規劃方向與政策建議中，納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議，⁸ 即一項旨在投入 20% 資源以支持原住民族與地方社區之願景目標，並加強對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的支持（其願景基準為 35%），以及引入旨在動員私募資本之 25% 投入的願景目標；","html":"<p>9.<br />\n亦<strong>歡迎</strong>在全球環境基金第九次增額期間的規劃方向與政策建議中，納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議，⁸ 即一項旨在投入 20% 資源以支持原住民族與地方社區之願景目標，並加強對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的支持（其願景基準為 35%），以及引入旨在動員私募資本之 25% 投入的願景目標；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"10. 進一步**歡迎**根據決議 16/33，在全球環境基金第九次增額下，成立全球環境基金理事會之特別治理工作小組；","html":"<p>10. 進一步<strong>歡迎</strong>根據決議 16/33，在全球環境基金第九次增額下，成立全球環境基金理事會之特別治理工作小組；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"[11. **請求**全球環境基金理事會考慮[於 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 第 21 段所列之][及決議 17/--]之標準，確保建立一個公平、公正、包容、高效且具代表性的民主透明治理系統[, 並促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的全面且有效參與]；]","html":"<p>[11. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金理事會考慮[於 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 第 21 段所列之][及決議 17/--]之標準，確保建立一個公平、公正、包容、高效且具代表性的民主透明治理系統[, 並促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的全面且有效參與]；]</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"12. **請求**全球環境基金加速其進一步強化效能之努力，包括透過以下方式：\n(a) 改進整合路徑、方法與整合計畫，以提供全系統之環境效益，從而增進環境公約間的綜效，同時確保此類計畫考量其各自之職權，保持由國家驅動，並回應國家情況與優先事項，且透過與受援國國家執行機構之實質參與來實施；\n(b) 透過其混合金融計畫之資助窗口，並向符合條件之締約方提供可預測之支持，來啟動並促進與《公約》目標一致之私部門融資，旨在開發能實現更大規模私營部門投資與金融流動之專案與計畫，","html":"<p>12. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金加速其進一步強化效能之努力，包括透過以下方式：<br />\n(a) 改進整合路徑、方法與整合計畫，以提供全系統之環境效益，從而增進環境公約間的綜效，同時確保此類計畫考量其各自之職權，保持由國家驅動，並回應國家情況與優先事項，且透過與受援國國家執行機構之實質參與來實施；<br />\n(b) 透過其混合金融計畫之資助窗口，並向符合條件之締約方提供可預測之支持，來啟動並促進與《公約》目標一致之私部門融資，旨在開發能實現更大規模私營部門投資與金融流動之專案與計畫，</p>","en":[10,11,12]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[]},{"md":"⁶ CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1。\n⁷ 決議 16/33，附件 I。\n⁸ 在先前規模擴大至 1 億美元的包容性保育倡議基礎上，","html":"<p>⁶ CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1。<br />\n⁷ 決議 16/33，附件 I。<br />\n⁸ 在先前規模擴大至 1 億美元的包容性保育倡議基礎上，</p>","en":[13,14,15,16]}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p003.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"private sector investment and financial flows, including through long-term enabling policy frameworks, incentives, regulations, blended finance tools and the development of financially viable, investment-ready biodiversity finance projects and pipelines, while recognizing that such investments complement public finance;"},{"t":"(c) Promoting whole-of-society and whole-of-government approaches, as appropriate and in accordance with national circumstances, to strengthen programme and project ownership at the national level and the alignment of biodiversity actions with nationally identified priorities, national biodiversity strategies and action plans, national development priorities, and policy coherence;"},{"t":"(d) Continuing to improve its system of resource allocation[9] [[, including by continuing to maximize the generation of global environmental benefits and recognizing the role of indigenous peoples and local communities in achieving them, and to improve the allocation performance of its implementing entities] [by enhancing transparency, equity, predictability and responsiveness to the [relevant][specific] needs and priorities of developing country Parties, including small island developing States and least developed countries]];"},{"t":"(e) Sustaining enhanced support for all eligible Parties, in particular least developed countries, small island developing States [and the most environmentally vulnerable countries], by reducing transaction costs, simplifying access procedures across existing Global Environment Facility focal areas and financing windows[, including through direct access modalities via national implementing agencies,] and improving the timeliness and predictability of financial support, measured by the date of first disbursement to the recipient country;"},{"t":"(f) Deepening accessible support for indigenous peoples and local communities, in line with element 8 of the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities to 203010 (access, including direct access, to funding for indigenous peoples and local communities for the conservation, restoration and sustainable use of biodiversity), including by developing guidance on the 20 per cent portfolio-wide target for indigenous peoples and local communities, which includes the [dedicated][[direct] access][11] modalities;"},{"t":"[(g) Strengthening the full, equitable, inclusive, effective and gender-responsive participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth[, including in decisionmaking,] in accordance with the national legislation of concerned Parties;]"},{"t":"(h) Continuing to promote country-driven national initiatives and regionally coordinated regional and multi-country initiatives[, including transboundary initiatives, with effective participation [and formal approval] [of national focal points for the Convention and relevant national authorities] [and formal approval of operational focal points for the Global Environment Facility]];"},{"t":"(i) Ensuring that Global Environment Facility support for the implementation of the Convention[, including support [through direct access [ 12 ]] for the implementation, monitoring, update and review of national biodiversity strategies and action plans,] is country-led and aligned with [national biodiversity strategies and action plans and] the targets of the Framework;"},{"t":"[9 Ensuring that any performance-based element of the allocation formula, including any measure of past disbursement, does not disadvantage Parties the disbursement rates of which reflect the capacity constraints that the financial mechanism exists to relieve, consistent with paragraph 4 of Article 20 of the Convention.]"},{"t":"10 Decision 16/4, annex."},{"t":"[11 Direct access for organizations of indigenous peoples and local communities include application of procedures for screening the capacities, experience and performance of organizations in managing funds and implementing projects, according to established Global Environment Facility procedures and following approval by the operational focal points of the Global Environment Facility, which is granted in coordination with the national focal point for the Convention.] 12 [Direct access for organizations of indigenous peoples and local communities include application of procedures for screening the capacities, experience and performance of organizations in managing funds and implementing projects, according to established Global Environment Facility procedures and following approval by the operational focal points of the Global Environment Facility, which is granted in coordination with the national focal point for the Convention.]"},{"t":"3/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"包括透過長期使能政策框架、激勵措施、法規、混合金融工具，以及開發具財務可行性且具投資準備度的生物多樣性金融計畫與案源；同時承認此類投資與公共財政互補；\n(c) 在適當且符合國家情況下，促進全社會與全政府方法，以強化國家層級的計畫與專案自主權，並使生物多樣性行動與國家認定的優先事項、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家發展優先事項以及政策一致性保持一致；\n(d) 持續改善其資源配置系統[9] [[，包括透過持續極大化全球環境效益的產生，並承認原住民族與地方社區在實現這些效益中所扮演的角色，以及改善其執行實體之配置績效] [藉由增進透明度、公平性、可預測性，並對開發中國家締約方（包括小島嶼開發中國家與低度開發國家）之[相關][特定]需求與優先事項之回應能力]]；\n(e) 透過降低交易成本、簡化現有全球環境基金焦點領域與融資窗口之取得程序[, 包括透過國家執行機構之直接取得模式，] 並改善財務支援的及時性與可預測性（以撥付至受援國之首筆款項日期為衡量標準），以持續為所有符合資格之締約方，特別是對於低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家[及環境最脆弱之國家]，提供強化之支援；\n(f) 深化對原住民族與地方社區之可取得支援，以符合第八條 (j) 工作計畫之第八要素，以及公約中其他與原住民族與地方社區相關之規定至 2030 年$^{10}$（包括對原住民族與地方社區用於生物多樣性保育、復育與永續利用之資金取得，包含直接取得），包括透過針對原住民族與地方社區 20% 全組合目標制定指南，其中包含[專屬][[直接]取得][11]模式；\n[(g) 根據相關締約方之國內立法，強化原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之全面、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應之參與[, 包括在決策過程中的參與；] ]\n(h) 持續促進由國家驅動之國家倡議，以及區域性且多國協調之區域與多國倡議[, 包括跨境倡議，並具備[公約國家焦點與相關國家主管機關之有效參與 [與正式核准] [以及全球環境基金執行焦點之正式核准]] ]；\n(i) 確保全球環境基金對執行公約之支援[, 包括[透過直接取得 [12] ]，以支援國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之執行、監測、更新與審查，] 是由國家主導，並與[國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫以及]綱要之目標保持一致；","html":"<p>包括透過長期使能政策框架、激勵措施、法規、混合金融工具，以及開發具財務可行性且具投資準備度的生物多樣性金融計畫與案源；同時承認此類投資與公共財政互補；<br />\n(c) 在適當且符合國家情況下，促進全社會與全政府方法，以強化國家層級的計畫與專案自主權，並使生物多樣性行動與國家認定的優先事項、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家發展優先事項以及政策一致性保持一致；<br />\n(d) 持續改善其資源配置系統[9] [[，包括透過持續極大化全球環境效益的產生，並承認原住民族與地方社區在實現這些效益中所扮演的角色，以及改善其執行實體之配置績效] [藉由增進透明度、公平性、可預測性，並對開發中國家締約方（包括小島嶼開發中國家與低度開發國家）之[相關][特定]需求與優先事項之回應能力]]；<br />\n(e) 透過降低交易成本、簡化現有全球環境基金焦點領域與融資窗口之取得程序[, 包括透過國家執行機構之直接取得模式，] 並改善財務支援的及時性與可預測性（以撥付至受援國之首筆款項日期為衡量標準），以持續為所有符合資格之締約方，特別是對於低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家[及環境最脆弱之國家]，提供強化之支援；<br />\n(f) 深化對原住民族與地方社區之可取得支援，以符合第八條 (j) 工作計畫之第八要素，以及公約中其他與原住民族與地方社區相關之規定至 2030 年<sup>10</sup>（包括對原住民族與地方社區用於生物多樣性保育、復育與永續利用之資金取得，包含直接取得），包括透過針對原住民族與地方社區 20% 全組合目標制定指南，其中包含[專屬][[直接]取得][11]模式；<br />\n[(g) 根據相關締約方之國內立法，強化原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之全面、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應之參與[, 包括在決策過程中的參與；] ]<br />\n(h) 持續促進由國家驅動之國家倡議，以及區域性且多國協調之區域與多國倡議[, 包括跨境倡議，並具備[公約國家焦點與相關國家主管機關之有效參與 [與正式核准] [以及全球環境基金執行焦點之正式核准]] ]；<br />\n(i) 確保全球環境基金對執行公約之支援[, 包括[透過直接取得 [12] ]，以支援國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之執行、監測、更新與審查，] 是由國家主導，並與[國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫以及]綱要之目標保持一致；</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"[9 確保分配公式中任何以績效為基礎之要素（包括任何對過去撥款量的衡量），不會對其撥款率反映出財務機制旨在緩解之能力限制的締約方造成不利，此應與公約第二十條第四段保持一致。]\n10 決議 16/4，附件。\n[11 原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織管理資金與執行專案之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序，並在與公約國家焦點協調下，經全球環境基金執行焦點核准後進行。]\n12 [原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織管理資金與執行專案之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序，並在與公約國家焦點協調下，經全球環境基金執行焦點核准後進行。]","html":"<p>[9 確保分配公式中任何以績效為基礎之要素（包括任何對過去撥款量的衡量），不會對其撥款率反映出財務機制旨在緩解之能力限制的締約方造成不利，此應與公約第二十條第四段保持一致。]<br />\n10 決議 16/4，附件。<br />\n[11 原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織管理資金與執行專案之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序，並在與公約國家焦點協調下，經全球環境基金執行焦點核准後進行。]<br />\n12 [原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，申請對組織管理資金與執行專案之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序，並在與公約國家焦點協調下，經全球環境基金執行焦點核准後進行。]</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]},{"md":"3/13","html":"<p>3/13</p>","en":[12]}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p004.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"(j) Continuing to support the development and implementation of national biodiversity finance plans or similar instruments and their integration, where applicable, into national policies and priorities;"},{"t":"(k) Continuing to advance collaboration, coherence and complementarity across multilateral climate funds and other sources of finance relevant to the implementation of the Framework;"},{"t":"(l) Strengthening national institutional and technical capacities for project preparation, implementation, monitoring and reporting;"},{"t":"[(m) Simplifying project development guidance;]"},{"t":"(n) Reporting on the attainment of the targets mentioned in paragraph 9 above and on disaggregated data on programming, approvals and disbursement by recipient country or region; [(o) Improving the transparency and granularity of reporting on biodiversity-related finance, including by distinguishing between financing for which biodiversity is a principal objective and financing for which it is a significant objective under the Rio marker methodology, taking into account the qualitative nature of the Rio markers and by clarifying the extent to which such financing contribute to the implementation of the Framework;]"},{"t":"[13. Also requests the Global Environment Facility to report to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting on the resources of the biodiversity focal area for the ninth replenishment period of its Trust Fund expressed in United States dollars at the final replenishment level, together with the corresponding figure for the eighth replenishment period, and on the share of resources originally programmed and subsequently disbursed to small island developing States, presented separately from least developed countries;]"},{"t":"14. Recognizes the value of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund in complementing the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund by providing financial support to eligible developing country Parties for achieving the goals and targets of the Framework;"},{"t":"[15. Expresses its appreciation [to the Global Environment Facility] for the operationalization of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund in record time with a streamlined project cycle[, the demonstration of speed of delivery] and the achievement to date of the three portfolio targets pertaining to least developed countries and small islands developing States, indigenous peoples and local communities[, women and youth,] and resources programmed through international financial institutions;]"},{"t":"[16. Takes note [with deep concern] of the information on the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund contained in the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties[, in particular the limited scale of capitalization to date in relation to the financing needs for the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework][and that many eligible Parties have not yet received support from the Fund];]"},{"t":"17. Reiterates the call made by the Council of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund at its sixth meeting for new and additional contributions from all sources to support the continuous, rapid and robust capitalization of the Fund[, without prejudice to the obligations of developed country Parties under Article 20 of the Convention and with a view to attracting contributions from sovereign, non-sovereign, private sector, philanthropic and financial actors];"},{"t":"[18. Requests the Global Environment Facility to enhance efforts to mobilize predictable, adequate and additional resources from all sources and report on the implementation of the resource mobilization strategy for the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund for the period from July 2026 to June 2030, including through disaggregated information on pledges, commitments, [approvals, disbursements,] sources of finance, [financial instruments, concessionality,] co-financing, private 4/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"(j)\n持續支持國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具的制定與實施，並在適用情況下將其納入國家政策與優先事項；\n(k) 持續促進多邊氣候基金與其他與實施綱要相關之資金來源之間的協作、一致性與互補性；\n(l)\n強化國家在計畫準備、實施、監測與報告方面的制度與技術能力；\n[(m) 簡化計畫開發指南；]\n(n) 報告上述第 9 段所述目標之達成情況，以及按受援國家或區域分類之規劃、核准與撥款的細分資料；\n[(o) 提高生物多樣性相關財務報告的透明度與細粒度，包括根據里約標記（Rio marker）方法論，區分以生物多樣性為主要目標的融資與以生物多樣性為重要目標的融資，並考量里約標記的性質，並澄清此類融資對實施綱要的貢獻程度；]\n[13. 亦請求全球環境基金向第十八屆締約方大會報告，其信託基金第九期增資期間，以美元表示的生物多樣性重點領域資源於最終增補水平之金額，並附上第八期增資期間的對應數字，以及原先規劃並隨後撥款予小島嶼開發中國家的資源比例，且此項報告應與低度開發國家分開呈現；]\n14. 認可全球生物多樣性綱要基金在補充全球環境基金信託基金方面的價值，透過為符合條件的開發中國家締約方提供財務支持，以實現綱要的目標與指標；\n[15. 對於 [全球環境基金] 以精簡的計畫週期 [展現交付速度] 於創紀錄的時間內實現全球生物多樣性綱要基金的運作，以及迄今為止在涉及低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家、原住民族與地方社區[, 女性與青年,] 以及透過國際金融機構規劃之資源的三項投資組合目標之達成，表示感謝；]\n[16. [深感憂慮地] 注意到全球環境基金理事會在第十七屆締約方大會報告中所包含的關於全球生物多樣性綱要基金的資訊[, 特別是迄今為止的資本化規模相對於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之融資需求而言仍屬有限][且許多符合條件的締約方尚未從該基金獲得支持]；]\n17. 重申全球生物多樣性綱要基金理事會在第六次會議上所提出的呼籲，即要求來自所有來源的新增與額外貢獻，以支持基金持續、快速且穩健的資本化，[, 在不損害公約第二十條下已開發國家締約方義務的前提下，並旨在吸引來自主權、非主權、私營部門、慈善與金融行為者的貢獻];\n[18. 請求全球環境基金加強努力，從所有來源動員可預測、充足且額外的資源，並報告 2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月期間全球生物多樣性綱要基金資源動員策略的實施情況，包括透過認捐、承諾、[核准、撥款,] 資金來源、[金融工具、優惠性,] 共同融資、私營部門的細分資訊，","html":"<p>(j)<br />\n持續支持國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具的制定與實施，並在適用情況下將其納入國家政策與優先事項；<br />\n(k) 持續促進多邊氣候基金與其他與實施綱要相關之資金來源之間的協作、一致性與互補性；<br />\n(l)<br />\n強化國家在計畫準備、實施、監測與報告方面的制度與技術能力；<br />\n[(m) 簡化計畫開發指南；]<br />\n(n) 報告上述第 9 段所述目標之達成情況，以及按受援國家或區域分類之規劃、核准與撥款的細分資料；<br />\n[(o) 提高生物多樣性相關財務報告的透明度與細粒度，包括根據里約標記（Rio marker）方法論，區分以生物多樣性為主要目標的融資與以生物多樣性為重要目標的融資，並考量里約標記的性質，並澄清此類融資對實施綱要的貢獻程度；]<br />\n[13. 亦請求全球環境基金向第十八屆締約方大會報告，其信託基金第九期增資期間，以美元表示的生物多樣性重點領域資源於最終增補水平之金額，並附上第八期增資期間的對應數字，以及原先規劃並隨後撥款予小島嶼開發中國家的資源比例，且此項報告應與低度開發國家分開呈現；]<br />\n14. 認可全球生物多樣性綱要基金在補充全球環境基金信託基金方面的價值，透過為符合條件的開發中國家締約方提供財務支持，以實現綱要的目標與指標；<br />\n[15. 對於 [全球環境基金] 以精簡的計畫週期 [展現交付速度] 於創紀錄的時間內實現全球生物多樣性綱要基金的運作，以及迄今為止在涉及低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家、原住民族與地方社區[, 女性與青年,] 以及透過國際金融機構規劃之資源的三項投資組合目標之達成，表示感謝；]<br />\n[16. [深感憂慮地] 注意到全球環境基金理事會在第十七屆締約方大會報告中所包含的關於全球生物多樣性綱要基金的資訊[, 特別是迄今為止的資本化規模相對於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之融資需求而言仍屬有限][且許多符合條件的締約方尚未從該基金獲得支持]；]<br />\n17. 重申全球生物多樣性綱要基金理事會在第六次會議上所提出的呼籲，即要求來自所有來源的新增與額外貢獻，以支持基金持續、快速且穩健的資本化，[, 在不損害公約第二十條下已開發國家締約方義務的前提下，並旨在吸引來自主權、非主權、私營部門、慈善與金融行為者的貢獻];<br />\n[18. 請求全球環境基金加強努力，從所有來源動員可預測、充足且額外的資源，並報告 2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月期間全球生物多樣性綱要基金資源動員策略的實施情況，包括透過認捐、承諾、[核准、撥款,] 資金來源、[金融工具、優惠性,] 共同融資、私營部門的細分資訊，</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p005.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"sector contributions and non-sovereign contributions and the extent to which resources are new and additional;]"},{"t":"[19. Invites developed country Parties and Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of developed country Parties, other governments at all levels, the private sector and philanthropic organizations to make or increase their contributions to the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund;] [20. Requests the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund and its implementing agencies to[, where appropriate,] [continue to]:"},{"t":"[(a) Facilitate, as appropriate and on a voluntary basis, the broadening of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund contributor base and the mobilization of additional financial resources;]"},{"t":"[(b) Improve co-financing arrangements, without making co-financing a condition for access to Global Biodiversity Framework Fund resources and in a manner that does not create additional barriers to access for developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries [,][and] small island developing States [and the most environmentally vulnerable countries], or shift the financial burden to recipient countries;]"},{"t":"[(c) Simplify and expedite project approval and disbursement procedures, including the endorsement process and disbursement processes for approved projects under the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund[, without prejudice to country ownership];]"},{"t":"[(d)"},{"t":"Simplify implementation procedures[, where appropriate];]"},{"t":"[(e)"},{"t":"Reduce project cycle processing times;]"},{"t":"[(f) Report on processing and disbursement times disaggregated for least developed countries and small island developing States;]"},{"t":"[(g) Provide necessary resources, fully disbursed allocated funds and complete organizational work, including at the national level, in support of the preparation of the eighth national reports by the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;] [(h) Enhance equitable access, including by considering measures to facilitate access for eligible country Parties that have not yet received support from the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund;]]"},{"t":"21. Requests the Global Environment Facility, in collaboration with the Executive Secretary of the Convention[, to consider supporting,][to provide support to] [all] eligible Parties in line with its mandate, for:"},{"t":"(a) [National platforms or ]existing national coordination mechanisms designed to aid project preparation, as necessary[, and track ongoing biodiversity funding needs, gaps and priorities;] [(b) Capacity-building and readiness support for national implementing agencies, including for accreditation;]"},{"t":"(c) The preparation and submission of national reports on the implementation of the Convention, the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety13 and the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization, taking into account national circumstances;14"},{"t":"(d) Capacity-building for leveraging private sector financing, including from capital markets, through, inter alia, innovative mechanisms and blended finance, and for developing financially viable projects, with robust safeguards[ to avoid increasing debt vulnerabilities];"},{"t":"13 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"14 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619."},{"t":"5/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"部門貢獻與非主權貢獻，以及資源在多大程度上屬於新增且額外的資源；]","html":"<p>部門貢獻與非主權貢獻，以及資源在多大程度上屬於新增且額外的資源；]</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"[19. **邀請**已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方、各級其他政府、私營部門及慈善組織，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行或增加其貢獻；]","html":"<p>[19. <strong>邀請</strong>已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方、各級其他政府、私營部門及慈善組織，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行或增加其貢獻；]</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"[20. **請求**全球生物多樣性綱要基金及其執行機構[, 在適當情況下,] [繼續]：\n[(a) 在適當且基於自願的基礎上，促進全球生物多樣性綱要基金捐助者基礎的擴大以及額外財務資源的動員；]\n[(b) 改進共同融資安排，但不將共同融資作為取得全球生物多樣性綱要基金資源的條件，且其方式不應為開發中締約方（特別是低度開發國家[,][及]小島嶼開發中國家[以及環境最脆弱的國家]）增加額外的取得障礙，亦不應將財務負擔轉嫁至受援國；]\n[(c) 簡化並加速專案核准與撥款程序，包括全球生物多樣性綱要基金下已核准專案的認可程序與撥款程序[, 在不損害國家自主權的前提下]；]\n[(d) 簡化執行程序[, 在適當情況下]；]\n[(e) 縮短專案週期處理時間；]\n[(f) 針對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，分別報告處理與撥款時間；]\n[(g) 提供必要資源、全額撥付已分配資金並完成組織工作（包括在國家層級），以支持在第十八次締約方大會召開前完成第八次國家報告的準備工作；]\n[(h) 強化公平取得，包括考慮採取措施，以促進尚未獲得全球生物多樣性綱要基金支持之合資格締約方的取得；]]","html":"<p>[20. <strong>請求</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金及其執行機構[, 在適當情況下,] [繼續]：<br />\n[(a) 在適當且基於自願的基礎上，促進全球生物多樣性綱要基金捐助者基礎的擴大以及額外財務資源的動員；]<br />\n[(b) 改進共同融資安排，但不將共同融資作為取得全球生物多樣性綱要基金資源的條件，且其方式不應為開發中締約方（特別是低度開發國家[,][及]小島嶼開發中國家[以及環境最脆弱的國家]）增加額外的取得障礙，亦不應將財務負擔轉嫁至受援國；]<br />\n[(c) 簡化並加速專案核准與撥款程序，包括全球生物多樣性綱要基金下已核准專案的認可程序與撥款程序[, 在不損害國家自主權的前提下]；]<br />\n[(d) 簡化執行程序[, 在適當情況下]；]<br />\n[(e) 縮短專案週期處理時間；]<br />\n[(f) 針對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，分別報告處理與撥款時間；]<br />\n[(g) 提供必要資源、全額撥付已分配資金並完成組織工作（包括在國家層級），以支持在第十八次締約方大會召開前完成第八次國家報告的準備工作；]<br />\n[(h) 強化公平取得，包括考慮採取措施，以促進尚未獲得全球生物多樣性綱要基金支持之合資格締約方的取得；]]</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]},{"md":"21. **請求**全球環境基金與公約執行秘書合作[, 考慮支持，][提供支持予] [所有] 合資格締約方，並符合其職權範圍，以用於：\n(a) [國家平台或] 現有的旨在協助專案準備之國家協調機制，於必要時[, 並追蹤持續進行中的生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項；]\n[(b) 針對國家執行機構之能力建構與準備支持，包括用於認證之支持；]\n(c) 考量國家情況，編製並提交關於履行公約、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書¹³以及《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書》之國家報告；¹⁴\n(d) 透過（除其他方式外）創新機制與混合融資，強化利用私營部門融資（包括來自資本市場之融資）之能力建構與準備工作，以及開發具財務可行性且具備穩健保障措施之專案[以避免增加債務脆弱性]；","html":"<p>21. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金與公約執行秘書合作[, 考慮支持，][提供支持予] [所有] 合資格締約方，並符合其職權範圍，以用於：<br />\n(a) [國家平台或] 現有的旨在協助專案準備之國家協調機制，於必要時[, 並追蹤持續進行中的生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項；]<br />\n[(b) 針對國家執行機構之能力建構與準備支持，包括用於認證之支持；]<br />\n(c) 考量國家情況，編製並提交關於履行公約、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書¹³以及《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書》之國家報告；¹⁴<br />\n(d) 透過（除其他方式外）創新機制與混合融資，強化利用私營部門融資（包括來自資本市場之融資）之能力建構與準備工作，以及開發具財務可行性且具備穩健保障措施之專案[以避免增加債務脆弱性]；</p>","en":[12,13,14,15]},{"md":"¹³ 聯合國，《聯合國條約集》，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n¹⁴ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p>¹³ 聯合國，《聯合國條約集》，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n¹⁴ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[16,17,18]}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p006.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"22. Requests the Executive Secretary to undertake preparatory work for the stocktake review of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund referred to in paragraph 29 of decision 15/15,[ in accordance with annex III to the present decision], in conjunction with its seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, [recognizing that the stocktake shall inform, but not prejudge, consideration by the Conference of the Parties of the future institutional structure of the financial mechanism provided under Article 21 of the Convention];"},{"t":"[23. Invites the Global Environment Facility to facilitate financial support for eligible Parties that have not yet received support for the development of the national biodiversity strategies and action plans and national targets or the preparation of national reports;]"},{"t":"[24. Requests the Global Environment Facility, in consultation with recipient countries and the Executive Secretary, to review the effectiveness of projects funded during its seventh and eighth cycles for the development of national biodiversity strategies and actions plans and national reports [under the Convention and its Protocols] and to report on the measures that it has taken to address identified challenges [for][to adjust accordingly] the preparation of the eight national report [to the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before][at] the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;]"},{"t":"25. [Requests that specific resources be reserved for][Encourages developing country Parties to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety to submit to the Global Environment Facility] biosafety projects under the Protocol, given the small number of such projects funded in previous rounds;"},{"t":"26. Requests the Executive Secretary, in consultation with the Secretariat of the Global Environment Facility, to prepare a draft four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols related to the use of Facility resources for biodiversity for the period from July 2030 to June 2034, taking into consideration the global review of collective progress in the implementation of the Framework, [and addressing expressly the access modalities and capacity constraints of developing countries Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States, consistent with paragraphs 5 and 6 of Article 20 of the Convention,] for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties and subsequent adoption by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;"},{"t":"[27. Emphasizes that the preparation of the four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund is without prejudice to the process established in decision 16/34 regarding the institutional structure for the financial mechanism provided under Article 21 of the Convention.]"},{"t":"28. Adopts the additional guidance to the Global Environment Facility contained in annex I to the present decision, and requests the Council of the Global Environment Facility to include information regarding the implementation of the additional guidance in its reports to the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"29. Notes the information on funding needs received from 45 eligible Parties and the compilation and analysis of that information transmitted by the Secretariat of the Convention on Biological Diversity to the Global Environment Facility to help with the negotiations for the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund;"},{"t":"30. Takes note of the report on the assessment of the amount of funds needed for the implementation of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund;15"},{"t":"15 CBD/SBI/6/INF/13."},{"t":"6/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程第 8 (b) 項之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程第 8 (b) 項之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"22. **請求**執行秘書[根據本決議附件 III]，配合對財務機制有效性進行之第七次四年一度審查，為決議 15/15 第 29 段所指之全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行清查審核之準備工作；[認可清查審核應為締約方大會對《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制未來制度結構之考量提供資訊，但不應預設其結果]；","html":"<p>22. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書[根據本決議附件 III]，配合對財務機制有效性進行之第七次四年一度審查，為決議 15/15 第 29 段所指之全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行清查審核之準備工作；[認可清查審核應為締約方大會對《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制未來制度結構之考量提供資訊，但不應預設其結果]；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"[23. **邀請**全球環境基金促進對符合條件之締約方之財務支持，該等締約方尚未獲得用於制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家目標，或編製國家報告之支持；]","html":"<p>[23. <strong>邀請</strong>全球環境基金促進對符合條件之締約方之財務支持，該等締約方尚未獲得用於制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家目標，或編製國家報告之支持；]</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"[24. **請求**全球環境基金在諮詢受援國與執行秘書後，審查其第七與第八週期期間，為[在《公約》及其議定書下]制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告所資助之專案有效性，並報告其為[針對][相應調整]第八份國家報告之編製所採取之措施，[該報告應於第十八次締約方大會召開前之執行附屬機構會議][於第十八次締約方大會]提交；]","html":"<p>[24. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金在諮詢受援國與執行秘書後，審查其第七與第八週期期間，為[在《公約》及其議定書下]制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告所資助之專案有效性，並報告其為[針對][相應調整]第八份國家報告之編製所採取之措施，[該報告應於第十八次締約方大會召開前之執行附屬機構會議][於第十八次締約方大會]提交；]</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"25. [**請求保留特定資源用於**][**鼓勵卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之開發中國家締約方向全球環境基金提交**]議定書下之生物安全專案，鑑於先前輪次資助此類專案之數量較少；","html":"<p>25. [<strong>請求保留特定資源用於</strong>][<strong>鼓勵卡塔赫納生物安全議定書之開發中國家締約方向全球環境基金提交</strong>]議定書下之生物安全專案，鑑於先前輪次資助此類專案之數量較少；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"26. **請求**執行秘書在諮詢全球環境基金秘書處後，考量對《綱要》實施集體進展之全球審查，[並明確處理開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）之取得模式與能力限制，且與《公約》第 20 條第 5 及第 6 段一致]，為 2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月期間，準備一份以成果為導向之《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期框架草案，供執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議審議，並由締約方大會於其第十八次會議隨後採納，該框架應與使用基金資源用於生物多樣性之事項相關；","html":"<p>26. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在諮詢全球環境基金秘書處後，考量對《綱要》實施集體進展之全球審查，[並明確處理開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）之取得模式與能力限制，且與《公約》第 20 條第 5 及第 6 段一致]，為 2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月期間，準備一份以成果為導向之《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期框架草案，供執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議審議，並由締約方大會於其第十八次會議隨後採納，該框架應與使用基金資源用於生物多樣性之事項相關；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"[27. **強調**為全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期準備《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期成果導向框架，不影響決議 16/34 中關於《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制制度結構所建立之程序。]","html":"<p>[27. <strong>強調</strong>為全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期準備《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期成果導向框架，不影響決議 16/34 中關於《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制制度結構所建立之程序。]</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"28. **採納**本決議附件 I 中包含之給予全球環境基金之附加指南，並**請求**全球環境基金理事會在提交予締約方大會之報告中，納入有關執行該附加指南之資訊；","html":"<p>28. <strong>採納</strong>本決議附件 I 中包含之給予全球環境基金之附加指南，並<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金理事會在提交予締約方大會之報告中，納入有關執行該附加指南之資訊；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"29. **注意到**從 45 個符合條件之締約方收到之資金需求資訊，以及由生物多樣性公約秘書處傳送予全球環境基金之該等資訊之彙編與分析，以協助全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資之談判；","html":"<p>29. <strong>注意到</strong>從 45 個符合條件之締約方收到之資金需求資訊，以及由生物多樣性公約秘書處傳送予全球環境基金之該等資訊之彙編與分析，以協助全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資之談判；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"30. **注意到**關於為全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期實施《公約》及其議定書所需資金金額之評估報告；¹⁵","html":"<p>30. <strong>注意到</strong>關於為全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期實施《公約》及其議定書所需資金金額之評估報告；¹⁵</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[9]},{"md":"¹⁵ CBD/SBI/6/INF/13.","html":"<p>¹⁵ CBD/SBI/6/INF/13.</p>","en":[10,11]}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p007.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"31. Notes the limited number of submissions from eligible Parties and therefore limited information available for assessing the amount of funds needed for the implementation of the Convention and its Protocols and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework for the ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund; [32. Also notes the importance of a realistic assessment of funding necessary and available for the implementation of the Convention and its Protocols and the Framework for the ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility;]"},{"t":"[33. Emphasizes the need to strengthen technical and institutional support for eligible Parties, so that their needs are fully reflected in future assessments;]"},{"t":"[34. Adopts the terms of reference for a full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention for the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June 2034), as contained in annex II to the present decision, noting that the assessment should be conducted in a manner that avoids disproportionate administrative burdens and provides for financial and technical support for data collection in developing country Parties;] [35. Encourages Parties to establish national platforms for planning and monitoring biodiversity projects that and are accessible to stakeholders and regularly updated;] [36. Adopts the terms of reference for the seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, as contained in annex III to the present decision;]"},{"t":"37. Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations, as well as indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, to contribute to and participate in the seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, as outlined in the terms of reference;"},{"t":"38. Emphasizes the importance of integrating [in the quadrennial review] specific indicators for eligible Parties, in particular on the number of projects funded, disbursement times and impact on local communities;"},{"t":"39. Requests the Executive Secretary[, subject to availability of resources]:"},{"t":"[(a) To commission and make available a report on the seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism in time for consideration by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;]"},{"t":"(b) To prepare a report on the full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention for the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund, for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties and by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting; [(c) To further strengthen collaboration and engagement with financial institutions and stakeholders, especially those recognized by the Global Environment Facility, the Green Climate Fund and the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development, in order to accelerate the implementation of the Framework, with an emphasis on improving access modalities[, including direct access and [simplified][simplifying] procedures for developing country Parties], while ensuring transparency, accountability, gender equality and the respect for human rights;]"},{"t":"7/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"31. **注意到**符合資格之締約方提交的報告數量有限，因此對於評估全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，為執行《公約》及其議定書以及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》所需資金金額之可用資訊有限；","html":"<p>31. <strong>注意到</strong>符合資格之締約方提交的報告數量有限，因此對於評估全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，為執行《公約》及其議定書以及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》所需資金金額之可用資訊有限；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"[32. **亦注意到**對於全球環境基金第九期增資期間，針對執行《公約》及其議定書與《綱要》所需且可用資金進行務實評估之重要性；]","html":"<p>[32. <strong>亦注意到</strong>對於全球環境基金第九期增資期間，針對執行《公約》及其議定書與《綱要》所需且可用資金進行務實評估之重要性；]</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"[33. **強調**有必要加強對符合資格締約方的技術與制度支持，以使其需求能充分反映在未來的評估中；]","html":"<p>[33. <strong>強調</strong>有必要加強對符合資格締約方的技術與制度支持，以使其需求能充分反映在未來的評估中；]</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"[34. **採納**如本決議附件 II 所載，關於針對開發中締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及轉型經濟體締約方，依據締約方所提供之指引，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在《公約》下承諾所需資金金額之全面評估工作說明書；並**注意到**該評估應以避免不成比例的行政負擔之方式進行，並為開發中締約方的資料收集提供財務與技術支持；]","html":"<p>[34. <strong>採納</strong>如本決議附件 II 所載，關於針對開發中締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及轉型經濟體締約方，依據締約方所提供之指引，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在《公約》下承諾所需資金金額之全面評估工作說明書；並<strong>注意到</strong>該評估應以避免不成比例的行政負擔之方式進行，並為開發中締約方的資料收集提供財務與技術支持；]</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"[35. **鼓勵**締約方建立用於規劃與監測生物多樣性計畫的國家平台，且該平台應為利害關係人所能使用並定期更新；]","html":"<p>[35. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方建立用於規劃與監測生物多樣性計畫的國家平台，且該平台應為利害關係人所能使用並定期更新；]</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"[36. **採納**如本決議附件 III 所載，關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之工作說明書；]","html":"<p>[36. <strong>採納</strong>如本決議附件 III 所載，關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之工作說明書；]</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"37. **邀請**締約方、其他政府與相關組織，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，參與並為工作說明書中所概述之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻；","html":"<p>37. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府與相關組織，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，參與並為工作說明書中所概述之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"38. **強調**在 [四年一度審查中] 納入符合資格締約方之特定指標的重要性，特別是關於資助計畫數量、撥款時間以及對地方社區之影響；","html":"<p>38. <strong>強調</strong>在 [四年一度審查中] 納入符合資格締約方之特定指標的重要性，特別是關於資助計畫數量、撥款時間以及對地方社區之影響；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"39. **請求**執行秘書[在資源可用之情況下]：","html":"<p>39. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書[在資源可用之情況下]：</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"[(a) 委託並提供一份關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之報告，以便締約方大會於其第十八次會議上進行審議；]","html":"<p>[(a) 委託並提供一份關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之報告，以便締約方大會於其第十八次會議上進行審議；]</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(b) 準備一份關於針對開發中締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及轉型經濟體締約方，依據締約方所提供之指引，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間履行其在《公約》下承諾所需資金金額之全面評估報告，供執行附屬機構於締約方大會第十八次會議召開前之會議上，以及締約方大會於其第十八次會議上進行審議；","html":"<p>(b) 準備一份關於針對開發中締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及轉型經濟體締約方，依據締約方所提供之指引，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間履行其在《公約》下承諾所需資金金額之全面評估報告，供執行附屬機構於締約方大會第十八次會議召開前之會議上，以及締約方大會於其第十八次會議上進行審議；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"[(c) 進一步加強與金融機構及利害關係人之合作與參與，特別是經全球環境基金、綠色氣候基金及經濟合作暨發展組織認可之機構，以加速《綱要》之實施，並著重於改善取得模式[包括開發中締約方的直接取得與 [簡化][簡化] 程序]，同時確保透明度、問責制、性別平等及對人權的尊重；]","html":"<p>[(c) 進一步加強與金融機構及利害關係人之合作與參與，特別是經全球環境基金、綠色氣候基金及經濟合作暨發展組織認可之機構，以加速《綱要》之實施，並著重於改善取得模式[包括開發中締約方的直接取得與 [簡化][簡化] 程序]，同時確保透明度、問責制、性別平等及對人權的尊重；]</p>","en":[8]}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p008.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"[(d) To report on the results of the collaboration and engagement mentioned in the subparagraph above, and include options for such engagements, to the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;] [(e) To facilitate the effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth in the implementation of the activities referred to in subparagraphs (a) to (d) above.]"},{"t":"Annex I"},{"t":"Additional guidance to the Global Environment Facility"},{"t":"[Placeholder for elements of guidance]"},{"t":"Annex II"},{"t":"Terms of reference for a full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention for the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June 2034)"},{"t":"A. Objective and scope"},{"t":"1. The objective of the work to be carried out under the present terms of reference is to enable the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity16 to make an assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention and its Protocols, in particular the commitment to implementing any successor to the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework 17 over the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June 2034), and determine the amount of resources needed, in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 21 of the Convention and decision III/8 of 15 November 1996 of the Conference of the Parties."},{"t":"B. Methodology"},{"t":"2. The funding needs assessment should be conducted taking into account:"},{"t":"(a) Article 20 and paragraph 1 of Article 21 of the Convention, as well as the Framework;"},{"t":"(b) Guidance provided to the financial mechanism by the Conference of the Parties, which may call for future financial resources, and in the resource mobilization decision, in which the Conference of the Parties calls for a broadening of the contributor base;"},{"t":"(c) All obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and relevant decisions adopted by the Conference of the Parties, in particular the Framework;"},{"t":"(d) National strategies, plans or programmes developed in accordance with Article 6 of the Convention and national biodiversity finance plans or similar instruments, where available;"},{"t":"(e) Information communicated to the Conference of the Parties in national reports and by the Parties through the financial reporting framework and other submission responses to surveys and interviews;"},{"t":"16 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"17 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"8/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"[(d) 向執行附屬機構報告上述次段落所述之合作與參與結果，並包含此類參與之選項，且該報告應於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議中提出；]\n[(e) 促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年有效參與上述 (a) 至 (d) 次段落所述活動之實施。]","html":"<p>[(d) 向執行附屬機構報告上述次段落所述之合作與參與結果，並包含此類參與之選項，且該報告應於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議中提出；]<br />\n[(e) 促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年有效參與上述 (a) 至 (d) 次段落所述活動之實施。]</p>","en":[1,2]},{"md":"附件 I\n給全球環境基金之額外指引\n[指引要素之佔位符]","html":"<p>附件 I<br />\n給全球環境基金之額外指引<br />\n[指引要素之佔位符]</p>","en":[3,4]},{"md":"附件 II\n根據締約方大會所提供之指引，針對為協助開發中締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及轉型經濟之締約方，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在《公約》下之承諾，進行所需資金總額之全面評估，其任務說明\nA.","html":"<p>附件 II<br />\n根據締約方大會所提供之指引，針對為協助開發中締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及轉型經濟之締約方，於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在《公約》下之承諾，進行所需資金總額之全面評估，其任務說明<br />\nA.</p>","en":[5,6]},{"md":"目標與範圍","html":"<p>目標與範圍</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"1.\n根據本任務說明所進行之工作，其目標在於使《生物多樣性公約》<sup>16</sup> 締約方大會能夠進行評估，以確定在履行其於《公約》及其議定書下之承諾（特別是履行《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》<sup>17</sup> 之任何後續文件之承諾），於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）內，依據締約方大會所提供之指引，協助開發中締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及轉型經濟之締約方所需之資金總額，並根據《公約》第 21 條第 1 段及 1996 年 11 月 15 日締約方大會決議 III/8，確定所需資源之數量。","html":"<p>1.<br />\n根據本任務說明所進行之工作，其目標在於使《生物多樣性公約》<sup>16</sup> 締約方大會能夠進行評估，以確定在履行其於《公約》及其議定書下之承諾（特別是履行《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》<sup>17</sup> 之任何後續文件之承諾），於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）內，依據締約方大會所提供之指引，協助開發中締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及轉型經濟之締約方所需之資金總額，並根據《公約》第 21 條第 1 段及 1996 年 11 月 15 日締約方大會決議 III/8，確定所需資源之數量。</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"B.","html":"<p>B.</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"方法論","html":"<p>方法論</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"2.\n資金需求評估應考量：\n(a) 《公約》第 20 條及第 21 條第 1 段，以及《綱要》；","html":"<p>2.<br />\n資金需求評估應考量：<br />\n(a) 《公約》第 20 條及第 21 條第 1 段，以及《綱要》；</p>","en":[10,11]},{"md":"(b) 締約方大會向財務機制提供之指引（該指引可能要求未來之財務資源），以及在要求擴大捐助者基礎之資源動員決議中之指引；\n(c) 《公約》及其議定書下之所有義務，以及締約方大會所通過之相關決議，特別是《綱要》；\n(d) 依據《公約》第 6 條所制定之國家策略、計畫或方案，以及國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具（若有）；\n(e) 透過國家報告向締約方大會傳達之資訊，以及締約方透過財務報告架構及對調查與訪談之其他提交回應所提供之資訊；","html":"<p>(b) 締約方大會向財務機制提供之指引（該指引可能要求未來之財務資源），以及在要求擴大捐助者基礎之資源動員決議中之指引；<br />\n(c) 《公約》及其議定書下之所有義務，以及締約方大會所通過之相關決議，特別是《綱要》；<br />\n(d) 依據《公約》第 6 條所制定之國家策略、計畫或方案，以及國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具（若有）；<br />\n(e) 透過國家報告向締約方大會傳達之資訊，以及締約方透過財務報告架構及對調查與訪談之其他提交回應所提供之資訊；</p>","en":[12,13,14]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[]},{"md":"<sup>16</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n<sup>17</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。","html":"<p><sup>16</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>17</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。</p>","en":[15,16,17,18]}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p009.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"(f) Policies and guidelines agreed by the Council of the Global Environment Facility for determining eligibility for funding of projects;"},{"t":"(g) Synergies with other biodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral environmental agreements funded by the Global Environment Facility, including those with respect to operations and impacts;"},{"t":"(h) Additional private capital mobilized through blended finance, including through the use of non-grant instruments, while recognizing the challenges that may be experienced by some Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, in mobilizing private capital in this regard;"},{"t":"(i) Policy coherence;"},{"t":"(j) Other relevant estimations, including the costs of implementing the Gender Plan of Action (2023–2030);18"},{"t":"[(k) Exchange rates, inflation volatility and the rising cost of conserving biodiversity in developing economies.]"},{"t":"3. In the context of the assessment, interviews, surveys, quantitative and qualitative analyses, and consultations should be undertaken, as needed for the preparation of the report, including:"},{"t":"(a) A compilation and analysis of the needs identified in national biodiversity strategies and action plans and national biodiversity finance plans, including country-specific resource mobilization strategies, prepared by Global Environment Facility-eligible and other relevant Parties pursuant to Article 6 of the Convention, taking into account incremental cost funding as the fundamental operational principle of the Global Environment Facility;"},{"t":"(b) A review of reports submitted by Parties pursuant to Articles 6 and 26 of the Convention, as well as Article 33 of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety19 and Article 29 of the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization, 20 to identify funding needs related to the fulfilment of their obligations under the Convention and its Protocols;"},{"t":"(c) The estimated financial implications of guidance provided to the financial mechanism by the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"(d) A compilation and analysis of any supplementary information provided by Global Environment Facility-eligible Parties on their funding needs for the implementation of their obligations under the Convention and its Protocols."},{"t":"C. Implementation"},{"t":"4. The national focal points of the Convention and the focal points of the financial mechanism [should][may], as appropriate, bear joint responsibility for coordinating national-level incremental funding needs assessments, in collaboration with relevant stakeholders and other focal points under the Convention and related conventions to ensure a whole-of-government approach."},{"t":"5. The national focal points may establish a national platform or use existing national coordination mechanisms, or both, to aid project planning, as necessary, and track ongoing biodiversity funding needs, gaps and priorities. Close links should be established between the national platform or relevant coordination mechanism and national support initiatives of relevant funding providers, in particular the country engagement strategy of the Global Environment Facility."},{"t":"18 Decision 15/11, annex."},{"t":"19 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"20 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619"},{"t":"9/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"(f)\n全球環境基金理事會所同意，用於判定計畫資助資格之政策與指南；\n(g) 與其他由全球環境基金資助之生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議之綜效，包括在運作與影響方面之綜效；\n(h) 透過混合金融（包括使用非撥款工具）所動員之額外私人資本，同時承認部分締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，在於此方面動員私人資本時可能面臨的挑戰；\n(i)\n政策一致性；","html":"<p>(f)<br />\n全球環境基金理事會所同意，用於判定計畫資助資格之政策與指南；<br />\n(g) 與其他由全球環境基金資助之生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議之綜效，包括在運作與影響方面之綜效；<br />\n(h) 透過混合金融（包括使用非撥款工具）所動員之額外私人資本，同時承認部分締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，在於此方面動員私人資本時可能面臨的挑戰；<br />\n(i)<br />\n政策一致性；</p>","en":[1,2,3]},{"md":"(j)\n其他相關估算，包括執行性別行動計畫（2023–2030）之成本；18\n[(k) 匯率、通貨膨脹波動以及開發中經濟體保育生物多樣性成本上升之情況。]","html":"<p>(j)<br />\n其他相關估算，包括執行性別行動計畫（2023–2030）之成本；18<br />\n[(k) 匯率、通貨膨脹波動以及開發中經濟體保育生物多樣性成本上升之情況。]</p>","en":[4,5,6]},{"md":"3.\n在評估脈絡下，應根據編製報告之需要，進行訪談、調查、定量與定性分析及諮詢，包括：\n(a) 彙編並分析依據《公約》第六條，由具備全球環境基金資助資格之締約方及其他相關締約方所編製之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家生物多樣性財務計畫中所識別之需求，包括特定國家之資源動員策略，並應將增量成本資助視為全球環境基金之基本運作原則；\n(b) 審查締約方依據《公約》第六條與第二十六條，以及《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》19 之第三十三條與《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其成果之名古屋議定書》20 之第二十九條所提交之報告，以識別與履行其在《公約》及其議定書下義務相關之資助需求；\n(c) 估算締約方大會向財務機制提供指引所產生的財務影響；\n(d) 彙編並分析具備全球環境基金資助資格之締約方，就履行其在《公約》及其議定書下義務之資助需求所提供之任何補充資訊。","html":"<p>3.<br />\n在評估脈絡下，應根據編製報告之需要，進行訪談、調查、定量與定性分析及諮詢，包括：<br />\n(a) 彙編並分析依據《公約》第六條，由具備全球環境基金資助資格之締約方及其他相關締約方所編製之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家生物多樣性財務計畫中所識別之需求，包括特定國家之資源動員策略，並應將增量成本資助視為全球環境基金之基本運作原則；<br />\n(b) 審查締約方依據《公約》第六條與第二十六條，以及《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》19 之第三十三條與《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其成果之名古屋議定書》20 之第二十九條所提交之報告，以識別與履行其在《公約》及其議定書下義務相關之資助需求；<br />\n(c) 估算締約方大會向財務機制提供指引所產生的財務影響；<br />\n(d) 彙編並分析具備全球環境基金資助資格之締約方，就履行其在《公約》及其議定書下義務之資助需求所提供之任何補充資訊。</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]},{"md":"C.\n實施","html":"<p>C.<br />\n實施</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"4.\n《公約》之國家聯絡點與財務機制之聯絡點[應][可]視情況共同負責協調國家層級之增量資助需求評估，並與相關利害關係人及《公約》與相關公約下之其他聯絡點合作，以確保採取全政府方法。","html":"<p>4.<br />\n《公約》之國家聯絡點與財務機制之聯絡點[應][可]視情況共同負責協調國家層級之增量資助需求評估，並與相關利害關係人及《公約》與相關公約下之其他聯絡點合作，以確保採取全政府方法。</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"5.\n國家聯絡點得視必要情況建立國家平台或利用現有之國家協調機制，或兩者兼具，以協助計畫規劃，並追蹤進行中之生物多樣性資助需求、缺口與優先事項。國家平台或相關協調機制，應與相關資助提供者之國家支持倡議建立緊密聯繫，特別是全球環境基金之國家參與策略。","html":"<p>5.<br />\n國家聯絡點得視必要情況建立國家平台或利用現有之國家協調機制，或兩者兼具，以協助計畫規劃，並追蹤進行中之生物多樣性資助需求、缺口與優先事項。國家平台或相關協調機制，應與相關資助提供者之國家支持倡議建立緊密聯繫，特別是全球環境基金之國家參與策略。</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"18 決議 15/11，附件。\n19 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n20 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p>18 決議 15/11，附件。<br />\n19 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n20 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[15,16,17,18]}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p010.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"[6. The national platform should also facilitate the participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth organizations and other relevant stakeholders, through a whole-ofsociety [and human rights-based] approach, as appropriate.]"},{"t":"7. The Executive Secretary should provide the information received from Parties without additional reporting obligations on funding needs through an online platform, subject to the availability of resources, to facilitate the visualization of biodiversity funding needs, gaps and priorities on an ongoing basis."},{"t":"8. The Executive Secretary should prepare a report on the full assessment, and the report should be submitted for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties, with a view to providing recommendations for consideration by the Conference of the Parties at that meeting."},{"t":"9. At its eighteenth meeting, the Conference of the Parties will be invited to take note of the estimated amount of funds that are necessary for the implementation of the Convention and its Protocols for the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund."},{"t":"Annex III"},{"t":"Terms of reference for the seventh quadrennial review"},{"t":"of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism"},{"t":"A. Objectives"},{"t":"1. In accordance with paragraph 3 of Article 21 of the Convention on Biological Diversity21 and building upon the experience of the past six reviews of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, the Conference of the Parties to the Convention will undertake its seventh review at its eighteenth meeting and take appropriate action to improve the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, as necessary. For that purpose, the following elements will be included in the review:"},{"t":"(a) The conformity of the activities of the Global Environment Facility, as the institutional structure operating the financial mechanism, with the guidance of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"(b) The effectiveness of the financial mechanism in providing financial resources to enable [all] eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition to meet the agreed full incremental costs to them of implementing measures through which they fulfil their obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and that generate global environmental benefits, and benefit from their provisions, taking into account the need for predictability, adequacy, accessibility and timely flow of funds, including the performance of the Global Environment Facility implementing agencies;"},{"t":"(c) The efficiency of the financial mechanism in providing financial resources and, in accordance with the guidance of the Conference of the Parties, overseeing, monitoring and evaluating the results of activities financed by its resources, including their social and gender- and equity-related outcomes and impacts, as relevant;"},{"t":"(d) The effectiveness of catalysing and enhancing national implementation measures in line with national priorities for achieving global biodiversity goals and targets, including those related to the Convention and its Protocols;"},{"t":"(e) The efficiency and effectiveness of the activities funded by the Global Environment Facility and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund for the implementation of the Convention and the achievement of its three objectives, as well as, as applicable, the implementation of its Protocols, taking into account the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"21 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"10/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"[6. 國家平台亦應透過適當之全社會 [及以人權為基礎] 方法，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關利害關係人之參與。]","html":"<p>[6. 國家平台亦應透過適當之全社會 [及以人權為基礎] 方法，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關利害關係人之參與。]</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"7.\n**執行秘書**應在資源可用之情況下，透過線上平台提供從締約方收到之資訊，且不增加關於資金需求的額外報告義務，以促進生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項之持續視覺化。","html":"<p>7.<br />\n<strong>執行秘書</strong>應在資源可用之情況下，透過線上平台提供從締約方收到之資訊，且不增加關於資金需求的額外報告義務，以促進生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項之持續視覺化。</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"8.\n**執行秘書**應準備一份完整評估報告，且該報告應提交予執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議，旨在為締約方大會於該次會議審議時提供建議。","html":"<p>8.<br />\n<strong>執行秘書</strong>應準備一份完整評估報告，且該報告應提交予執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議，旨在為締約方大會於該次會議審議時提供建議。</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"9.\n在第十八次會議期間，將**邀請**締約方大會注意到為全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期，執行本公約及其議定書所需之估算資金金額。","html":"<p>9.<br />\n在第十八次會議期間，將<strong>邀請</strong>締約方大會注意到為全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期，執行本公約及其議定書所需之估算資金金額。</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"附件 III\n財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍","html":"<p>附件 III<br />\n財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍</p>","en":[5,6,7]},{"md":"A.\n目標","html":"<p>A.<br />\n目標</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"1.\n根據《生物多樣性公約》第二十一條第三項$^21$並基於過去六次財務機制有效性審查之經驗，締約方大會將於其第十八次會議進行第七次審查，並於必要時採取適當行動以提高財務機制之有效性。為此，審查應包含下列要素：\n(a) 作為運作財務機制之制度結構，全球環境基金之活動是否符合締約方大會之指導；\n(b) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之有效性，以使[所有]符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及轉型經濟體締約方，能夠負擔其履行本公約及其議定書義務並產生全球環境效益之措施所產生的約定全額增量成本，並從其規定中獲益；此處應考慮資金之可預測性、充足性、可取得性及時流動之需求，包括全球環境基金執行機構之績效；\n(c) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之效率，且根據締約方之指導原則，對其資源所資助之活動結果進行監督、監測與評估，包括其相關之社會、性別及公平相關之成果與影響；\n(d) 在符合達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標之國家優先事項（包括與本公約及其議定書相關之目標）下，催化並強化國家執行措施之有效性；\n(e) 由全球環境基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助，用於執行本公約、達成其三大目標以及（如適用）執行其議定書之活動的效率與有效性，並應考慮締約方所提供之指導原則；","html":"<p>1.<br />\n根據《生物多樣性公約》第二十一條第三項<sup>21</sup>並基於過去六次財務機制有效性審查之經驗，締約方大會將於其第十八次會議進行第七次審查，並於必要時採取適當行動以提高財務機制之有效性。為此，審查應包含下列要素：<br />\n(a) 作為運作財務機制之制度結構，全球環境基金之活動是否符合締約方大會之指導；<br />\n(b) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之有效性，以使[所有]符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及轉型經濟體締約方，能夠負擔其履行本公約及其議定書義務並產生全球環境效益之措施所產生的約定全額增量成本，並從其規定中獲益；此處應考慮資金之可預測性、充足性、可取得性及時流動之需求，包括全球環境基金執行機構之績效；<br />\n(c) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之效率，且根據締約方之指導原則，對其資源所資助之活動結果進行監督、監測與評估，包括其相關之社會、性別及公平相關之成果與影響；<br />\n(d) 在符合達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標之國家優先事項（包括與本公約及其議定書相關之目標）下，催化並強化國家執行措施之有效性；<br />\n(e) 由全球環境基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助，用於執行本公約、達成其三大目標以及（如適用）執行其議定書之活動的效率與有效性，並應考慮締約方所提供之指導原則；</p>","en":[9,10,11,12,13]},{"md":"---\n$^{21}$ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>21</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[14,15,16]}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p011.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"(f) The efficiency and effectiveness of processes and procedures for the deployment and use of resources, including simplified procedures and access modalities;"},{"t":"(g) The effectiveness and efficiency of the support provided for the objectives of the Convention and its Protocols in synergy with the implementation of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements, in a manner that is consistent with the mandates of the respective agreements;"},{"t":"(h) The effectiveness in improving access to financial resources and trends associated with funding for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth to support the implementation of the objectives of the Convention and its Protocols;"},{"t":"(i) The efficiency of each of the implementing agencies of the Global Environment Facility in providing technical support and services to countries in their preparation of project proposals and the implementation of projects, including with regard to the timely disbursement of fund, fees and project management costs, use of international consultants and control of expenditure."},{"t":"B. Methodology"},{"t":"2. The review will cover all the activities of the institutional structure operating the financial mechanism, in particular for the period from 1 July 2022 to 30 June 2026."},{"t":"3. The review shall draw upon, inter alia, and in a balanced manner, the following sources of information:"},{"t":"(a) The reviews of effectiveness of the financial mechanism in implementing the Convention undertaken pursuant to the memorandum of understanding between the Conference of the Parties to the Convention and the Council of the Global Environment Facility, as contained in the annex to decision III/8 of 15 November 1996;"},{"t":"(b) Reports prepared by the Global Environment Facility, including its reports for meetings of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention;"},{"t":"(c) Reports of the Independent Evaluation Office of the Global Environment Facility that relate to the biodiversity-related activities of the Facility, including the eighth comprehensive evaluation of the Global Environment Facility, as well as relevant assessments by the agencies accredited by the Council of the Facility and other partners;"},{"t":"[(d) The Multilateral Performance Network assessments of the Global Environment Facility and reports related to the review of the vertical climate and environmental funds under the Group of 20;22]"},{"t":"(e) Information regarding the financial mechanism provided by Parties through national reports and other submissions, surveys and interviews;"},{"t":"(f) Information provided by indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth and relevant stakeholders related to projects funded through the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, including their views on possible impacts on their rights, as applicable, as well as documented evidence and assessments of such impacts, including gender-differentiated impacts;"},{"t":"(g) Experience with, and lessons learned from, relevant international financial mechanisms;"},{"t":"(h) The report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"22 See www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html."},{"t":"11/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"(f) 資源部署與使用的程序與流程之效率與效能，包括簡化程序與取得模式；\n(g) 在與其他相關多邊環境協議之執行保持協同，且與各自協議之授權一致之情況下，為落實本公約及其議定書目標所提供之支持，其效能與效率；\n(h) 改善取得財務資源之效能，以及與為支持落實本公約及其議定書目標之原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年所提供資金相關之趨勢；\n(i) 全球環境基金各執行機構在提供技術支持與服務以協助各國編制計畫提案及執行計畫方面之效率，包括關於資金、費用與計畫管理成本之及時撥付、國際顧問之使用以及支出之控管。","html":"<p>(f) 資源部署與使用的程序與流程之效率與效能，包括簡化程序與取得模式；<br />\n(g) 在與其他相關多邊環境協議之執行保持協同，且與各自協議之授權一致之情況下，為落實本公約及其議定書目標所提供之支持，其效能與效率；<br />\n(h) 改善取得財務資源之效能，以及與為支持落實本公約及其議定書目標之原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年所提供資金相關之趨勢；<br />\n(i) 全球環境基金各執行機構在提供技術支持與服務以協助各國編制計畫提案及執行計畫方面之效率，包括關於資金、費用與計畫管理成本之及時撥付、國際顧問之使用以及支出之控管。</p>","en":[2,3,4]},{"md":"B.","html":"<p>B.</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"方法論","html":"<p>方法論</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"2.\n本次審查將涵蓋執行財務機制之制度結構的所有活動，特別是自 2022 年 7 月 1 日至 2026 年 6 月 30 日期間。","html":"<p>2.<br />\n本次審查將涵蓋執行財務機制之制度結構的所有活動，特別是自 2022 年 7 月 1 日至 2026 年 6 月 30 日期間。</p>","en":[6,7]},{"md":"3.\n審查應以平衡方式，除其他外，利用下列資訊來源：\n(a) 根據 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8 附件所載，依據本公約締約方大會與全球環境基金理事會間之合作備忘錄，針對落實本公約之財務機制效能所進行之審查；\n(b) 由全球環境基金編製之報告，包括其為本公約締約方大會會議所編製之報告；\n(c) 全球環境基金獨立評估辦公室與基金生物多樣性相關活動有關之報告，包括全球環境基金第八次全面評估，以及由基金理事會認可之機構及其他合作夥伴所進行之相關評估；\n[(d) 多邊績效網絡對全球環境基金之評估，以及與二十國集團（G20）架構下垂直氣候與環境基金審查相關之報告；$^{22}$]\n(e) 締約方透過國家報告及其他提交文件、調查與訪談所提供關於財務機制之資訊；\n(f) 由原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人所提供，與透過全球環境基金信託基金及全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助之計畫相關之資訊，包括其對其權利可能受到的影響（如適用）之看法，以及此類影響（包括性別差異化影響）之文件證據與評估；\n(g) 相關國際財務機制之經驗與經驗教訓；\n(h) 全球環境基金理事會為第十七次締約方大會所編製之報告；","html":"<p>3.<br />\n審查應以平衡方式，除其他外，利用下列資訊來源：<br />\n(a) 根據 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8 附件所載，依據本公約締約方大會與全球環境基金理事會間之合作備忘錄，針對落實本公約之財務機制效能所進行之審查；<br />\n(b) 由全球環境基金編製之報告，包括其為本公約締約方大會會議所編製之報告；<br />\n(c) 全球環境基金獨立評估辦公室與基金生物多樣性相關活動有關之報告，包括全球環境基金第八次全面評估，以及由基金理事會認可之機構及其他合作夥伴所進行之相關評估；<br />\n[(d) 多邊績效網絡對全球環境基金之評估，以及與二十國集團（G20）架構下垂直氣候與環境基金審查相關之報告；<sup>22</sup>]<br />\n(e) 締約方透過國家報告及其他提交文件、調查與訪談所提供關於財務機制之資訊；<br />\n(f) 由原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人所提供，與透過全球環境基金信託基金及全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助之計畫相關之資訊，包括其對其權利可能受到的影響（如適用）之看法，以及此類影響（包括性別差異化影響）之文件證據與評估；<br />\n(g) 相關國際財務機制之經驗與經驗教訓；<br />\n(h) 全球環境基金理事會為第十七次締約方大會所編製之報告；</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]},{"md":"$^{22}$ 參閱 www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html。","html":"<p><sup>22</sup> 參閱 www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html。</p>","en":[13,14,15,16,17]}]},{"p":"p012","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p012.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"(i) The stocktake review of the operations and performance of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund regarding its scale, speed and accessibility and the future arrangements requested in decision 15/15 of 19 December 2022."},{"t":"C. Criteria"},{"t":"[4."},{"t":"The effectiveness and efficiency of the financial mechanism should be assessed taking into account, inter alia:]"},{"t":"(a) The actions taken by the Global Environment Facility in response to the guidance of the Conference of the Parties and to the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework,23 including through the decisions of the Global Environment Facility Council on relations with conventions and international institutions;"},{"t":"(b) The extent to which eligible Parties[, including developing countries, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition] take measures to apply for and receive timely, adequate and predictable funding to enable them to meet the agreed full incremental cost to them of implementing measures through which they fulfil their obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and that generate global environmental benefits;"},{"t":"[(c) Information provided by Parties in relation to their performance in delivering projects under the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, including on the effectiveness and efficiency of access modalities, constraints affecting women’s access to financing, the competence and capacity of recipient Parties to maintain those modalities and the performance of implementing agencies;]"},{"t":"[(d) Percentage of eligible Parties that have received financial support from the financial mechanism for implementing global biodiversity goals and targets, including those related to the Convention and its Protocols;]"},{"t":"(e) Percentage of biodiversity-relevant funding through the financial mechanism in support of the achievement of global biodiversity goals and targets;"},{"t":"(f) Trends in co-financing, in particular private and non-grant financing in the biodiversity focal area enabled by the financial mechanism;"},{"t":"(g) Trends in financing global, regional and subregional biodiversity projects under the financial mechanism;"},{"t":"(h) Trends in financing that take into consideration synergies among conventions for which the Global Environment Facility has been designated to operate their financial mechanism on an ongoing and interim basis;"},{"t":"(i) Trends in financing targeted at biodiversity-related conventions and agreements taking into consideration synergies among them;"},{"t":"[(j) Trends in time frames for project development and resource disbursement, including the time between the approval of the concept note (or the project identification form) and the [first disbursement][moment the recipient country received the resources];]"},{"t":"[(k) Trends in financing targeted at or led by indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth and that respect, protect and fulfil human rights, including [direct] access to finance;]"},{"t":"[(l) Trends in the number and themes of capacity-building activities that enable Parties and stakeholders to secure access to financing from the Global Environment Facility;]"},{"t":"23 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"12/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"(i)\n針對全球生物多樣性綱要基金在規模、速度與可近性方面之運作與績效進行檢視，以及 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/15 所要求之未來安排。\nC.","html":"<p>(i)<br />\n針對全球生物多樣性綱要基金在規模、速度與可近性方面之運作與績效進行檢視，以及 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/15 所要求之未來安排。<br />\nC.</p>","en":[1,2]},{"md":"標準","html":"<p>標準</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"[4.\n應評估財務機制之有效性與效率，並應考量以下事項（包括但不限於）：]\n(a) 全球環境基金因應締約方大會之指引及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》$^{23}$ 所採取之行動，包括透過全球環境基金理事會關於與各公約及國際機構關係之決議；\n(b) 合格締約方[，包括開發中、特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方]採取措施申請並獲得及時、充足且可預測之資金之程度，以使其能夠負擔其履行《公約》及其議定書義務，且能產生全球環境效益之措施所產生的約定全額增量成本；\n[(c) 締約方就其執行全球環境基金信託基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金下專案之績效所提供之資訊，包括關於取得模式之有效性與效率、影響女性取得融資之限制、受援締約方維持該等模式之能力與職能，以及執行機構之績效；]\n[(d) 合格締約方中，已透過財務機制獲得資金支持以執行全球生物多樣性目標與指標（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標與指標）之百分比；]\n(e) 透過財務機制，用於支持達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標中，與生物多樣性相關之資金百分比；\n(f) 共同融資之趨勢，特別是透過財務機制在生物多樣性重點領域所促成之私人及非撥款型融資趨勢；\n(g) 在財務機制下，資助全球、區域及次區域生物多樣性專案之趨勢；\n(h) 考量各公約間綜效之融資趨勢，其中全球環境基金已被指定持續且臨時地負責執行該等公約之財務機制；\n(i) 考量各生物多樣性相關公約與協議間綜效之針對性融資趨勢；\n[(j) 專案開發與資源撥付時程之趨勢，包括概念說明書（或專案識別表）核准與[首次撥付][受援國收到資源之時刻]之間的時間；]\n[(k) 針對或由原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年所領導，且尊重、保護並履行人權之融資趨勢，包括[直接]取得融資之途徑；]\n[(l) 使締約方與利害關係人能夠確保取得全球環境基金融資之能力建構活動，其數量與主題之趨勢；]","html":"<p>[4.<br />\n應評估財務機制之有效性與效率，並應考量以下事項（包括但不限於）：]<br />\n(a) 全球環境基金因應締約方大會之指引及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》<sup>23</sup> 所採取之行動，包括透過全球環境基金理事會關於與各公約及國際機構關係之決議；<br />\n(b) 合格締約方[，包括開發中、特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方]採取措施申請並獲得及時、充足且可預測之資金之程度，以使其能夠負擔其履行《公約》及其議定書義務，且能產生全球環境效益之措施所產生的約定全額增量成本；<br />\n[(c) 締約方就其執行全球環境基金信託基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金下專案之績效所提供之資訊，包括關於取得模式之有效性與效率、影響女性取得融資之限制、受援締約方維持該等模式之能力與職能，以及執行機構之績效；]<br />\n[(d) 合格締約方中，已透過財務機制獲得資金支持以執行全球生物多樣性目標與指標（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標與指標）之百分比；]<br />\n(e) 透過財務機制，用於支持達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標中，與生物多樣性相關之資金百分比；<br />\n(f) 共同融資之趨勢，特別是透過財務機制在生物多樣性重點領域所促成之私人及非撥款型融資趨勢；<br />\n(g) 在財務機制下，資助全球、區域及次區域生物多樣性專案之趨勢；<br />\n(h) 考量各公約間綜效之融資趨勢，其中全球環境基金已被指定持續且臨時地負責執行該等公約之財務機制；<br />\n(i) 考量各生物多樣性相關公約與協議間綜效之針對性融資趨勢；<br />\n[(j) 專案開發與資源撥付時程之趨勢，包括概念說明書（或專案識別表）核准與[首次撥付][受援國收到資源之時刻]之間的時間；]<br />\n[(k) 針對或由原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年所領導，且尊重、保護並履行人權之融資趨勢，包括[直接]取得融資之途徑；]<br />\n[(l) 使締約方與利害關係人能夠確保取得全球環境基金融資之能力建構活動，其數量與主題之趨勢；]</p>","en":[4,5,6,7,8]},{"md":"$^{23}$ 決議 15/4，附件。","html":"<p><sup>23</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。</p>","en":[9,10,11,12,13]},{"md":"12/13","html":"<p>12/13</p>","en":[14,15,16,17,18]}]},{"p":"p013","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad648da49375d6d8008f62c/p013.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 8 (b) – 19 October 2026"},{"t":"[(m) Trends in project financing leading to high sustainability or durability ratings and longterm results achieved through biodiversity programming supported by the Global Environment Facility in relation to expected results planned by the Facility through that programming;] [(n)"},{"t":"Criteria listed in decision 16/34 of 27 February 2025.]"},{"t":"[5. The assessment should include a comparison of the Global Environment Facility with the financial mechanisms of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements, including the Green Climate Fund[,][ and] the Adaptation Fund [and the Fund for Responding to Loss and Damage]. Elements for consideration should include: contributor base; funding modalities and financial performance; criteria and processes for funding, including project cycle considerations; access and disbursement modalities (e.g. direct allocation or project-based disbursement), including for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth; relationship between the governing body of the fund and the Conference of the Parties to the respective multilateral environmental agreement; transparency, monitoring, reporting and evaluation; accreditation process and role and performance of implementing agencies; cost-effectiveness of operations; ability to leverage funding to mobilize additional finance for biodiversity; cost of setting up and running the financial instrument; leveraging public and private co-finance; and integration of various environmental fields.]"},{"t":"D. Procedures for implementation"},{"t":"[6. In consultation with the Bureau, the Executive Secretary will contract an experienced independent evaluator to undertake the review, in accordance with the aforementioned objectives, methodology and criteria.]"},{"t":"[7. The evaluator will undertake desk studies, questionnaire surveys, interviews and field visits, such as may be required for the implementation of the review, and collaborate for that purpose with the Global Environment Facility and its Independent Evaluation Office, as well as other independent assessments, such as those of the Multilateral Performance Network, if necessary, and prepare a compilation and synthesis of the information received.]"},{"t":"[8. Special efforts should be made to collect the views of Parties, the private sector, indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, including[, as applicable,] information on possible impacts on their rights [in relation to project-specific environmental objectives and in accordance with relevant national legislation].]"},{"t":"[9. The draft synthesis report and recommendations of the evaluator will be made available to the Global Environment Facility for its review and comments. Such comments will be included in the documentation and identified by source.]"},{"t":"[10. The report should include as an annex the study requested in paragraph 41 of decision 16/33 of 27 February 2025 benchmarking the Global Environment Facility against the financial mechanisms or similar instruments of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements, including with regard to their legal nature, funding modalities and financial performance, criteria and process for funding, access and disbursement modalities, monitoring and evaluation, governance and the cost-effectiveness of operations[, as well as other criteria contained in decision 16/34].] 10 bis."},{"t":"The report shall include as an annex the stocktake review referred to in decision 15/15."},{"t":"[11. On the basis of the synthesis report and recommendations of the independent evaluator, the Executive Secretary will prepare, in consultation with the Global Environment Facility, a draft decision on the seventh quadrennial review of the financial mechanism, including specific suggestions for action to improve the effectiveness of the mechanism[, if necessary,] for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation, with its recommendations to be submitted to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting.]"},{"t":"__________"},{"t":"13/13"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 8 (b) 之非正式文件 – 2026 年 10 月 19 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"[(m) 專案融資趨勢，其導致高永續性或耐久性評級，以及透過全球環境基金支持之生物多樣性計畫所達成之長期成果，與該基金透過該計畫預期達成之成果之關係；]\n[(n)\n2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 中所列之標準。]","html":"<p>[(m) 專案融資趨勢，其導致高永續性或耐久性評級，以及透過全球環境基金支持之生物多樣性計畫所達成之長期成果，與該基金透過該計畫預期達成之成果之關係；]<br />\n[(n)<br />\n2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 中所列之標準。]</p>","en":[1,2]},{"md":"[5. 評估應包含全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議財務機制之比較，包括綠色氣候基金[,][ 及] 適應基金 [以及損失與損害回應基金]。應考慮之要素應包括：出資者基礎；資金模式與財務績效；資助標準與程序，包括專案週期之考量；取得與撥付模式（例如：直接分配或以專案為基礎之撥付），包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之模式；基金管理機構與各自多邊環境協議締約方大會之間之關係；透明度、監測、報告與評估；認證程序以及執行機構之角色與績效；營運之成本效益；利用資金槓桿以動員額外生物多樣性資金之能力；建立與運行該財務工具之成本；槓桿化公共與私人共同融資；以及各種環境領域之整合。]","html":"<p>[5. 評估應包含全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議財務機制之比較，包括綠色氣候基金[,][ 及] 適應基金 [以及損失與損害回應基金]。應考慮之要素應包括：出資者基礎；資金模式與財務績效；資助標準與程序，包括專案週期之考量；取得與撥付模式（例如：直接分配或以專案為基礎之撥付），包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之模式；基金管理機構與各自多邊環境協議締約方大會之間之關係；透明度、監測、報告與評估；認證程序以及執行機構之角色與績效；營運之成本效益；利用資金槓桿以動員額外生物多樣性資金之能力；建立與運行該財務工具之成本；槓桿化公共與私人共同融資；以及各種環境領域之整合。]</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"D. 執行程序","html":"<p>D. 執行程序</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"[6. 執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，聘請一位經驗豐富的獨立評估員，根據前述目標、方法與標準進行審查。]\n[7. 評估員應進行書面研究、問卷調查、訪談與實地考察，例如為執行審查所必需之項目，並為此目的與全球環境基金及其獨立評估辦公室合作，必要時亦與其他獨立評估機構（如多邊績效網絡）合作，並編製所收資訊之彙編與綜合報告。]\n[8. 應特別努力收集締約方、私營部門、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年的意見，包括[, 如適用,] 關於其權利可能受影響之資訊 [與特定專案之環境目標相關，且符合相關國家立法]。]\n[9. 評估員之綜合報告草案與建議將提供予全球環境基金進行審查與評論。該等評論應納入文件中，並標明來源。]\n[10. 報告應包含一份附件，即 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/33 第 41 段所要求之研究，將全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議之財務機制或類似工具進行基準比較，包括其法律性質、資金模式與財務績效、資助標準與程序、取得與撥付模式、監測與評估、治理以及營運之成本效益[, 以及決議 16/34 中包含之其他標準]。]","html":"<p>[6. 執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，聘請一位經驗豐富的獨立評估員，根據前述目標、方法與標準進行審查。]<br />\n[7. 評估員應進行書面研究、問卷調查、訪談與實地考察，例如為執行審查所必需之項目，並為此目的與全球環境基金及其獨立評估辦公室合作，必要時亦與其他獨立評估機構（如多邊績效網絡）合作，並編製所收資訊之彙編與綜合報告。]<br />\n[8. 應特別努力收集締約方、私營部門、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年的意見，包括[, 如適用,] 關於其權利可能受影響之資訊 [與特定專案之環境目標相關，且符合相關國家立法]。]<br />\n[9. 評估員之綜合報告草案與建議將提供予全球環境基金進行審查與評論。該等評論應納入文件中，並標明來源。]<br />\n[10. 報告應包含一份附件，即 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/33 第 41 段所要求之研究，將全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議之財務機制或類似工具進行基準比較，包括其法律性質、資金模式與財務績效、資助標準與程序、取得與撥付模式、監測與評估、治理以及營運之成本效益[, 以及決議 16/34 中包含之其他標準]。]</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"10 bis.","html":"<p>10 bis.</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"報告應包含一份附件，即決議 15/15 中所提及之進度檢視審查。","html":"<p>報告應包含一份附件，即決議 15/15 中所提及之進度檢視審查。</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"[11. 執行秘書應根據獨立評估員之綜合報告與建議，並在諮詢全球環境基金後，準備一份關於財務機制第七次四年一度審查之決議草案，包括旨在提高機制有效性之具體行動建議[, 如有必要,]，以供執行附屬機構審議，其建議應提交至第十八次締約方大會。]\n__________\n13/13","html":"<p>[11. 執行秘書應根據獨立評估員之綜合報告與建議，並在諮詢全球環境基金後，準備一份關於財務機制第七次四年一度審查之決議草案，包括旨在提高機制有效性之具體行動建議[, 如有必要,]，以供執行附屬機構審議，其建議應提交至第十八次締約方大會。]</p>\n<hr />\n<p>13/13</p>","en":[11,12,13]}]}]};
